## Conversation
User asked to rebase PR #14965 (Mooncake Store shared-cache routing) on upstream/main and then address review feedback from dmitry-tokarev-nv. This commit addresses the first P2: learned-edge and digest maps never evicted, so the cache disabled itself permanently at either cap, and update_contract with the same contract did not clear `disabled`.

## Actions
Read vllm_mooncake_store.rs and its tests, mooncake_store_contract.rs (ValidatedContract fields), model_manager.rs MooncakeContractWatch (how update_contract is driven). Replaced `edges: FxHashMap` with `LruCache<Edge, LearnedEdge, FxBuildHasher>` (lru 0.16 already a dynamo-llm dep), unbounded with manual `pop_lru` at `limits.edges` so tests can override limits. Moved ambiguity to a separate `ambiguous: HashSet<u64>`; `DigestIdentity` now counts resident objects and is removed at zero; `clear_residency` also clears digests. Caps now clear residency and continue (the triggering event seeds the rebuild). Reverse-edge conflict marks the existing edge conflicted and refuses the new one, no disable. `disabled` is now only set when the subscriber stops. Wrote 5 new tests, adjusted 4 existing ones. Measured memory with a standalone counting-allocator program in the temp dir: 100.5 MiB live / 119 MiB peak at caps (LRU costs ~2 MiB over FxHashMap). Ran `cargo test -p dynamo-llm --no-default-features --lib` (2753 pass, 3 env failures), fmt, clippy.

## Errors & Mistakes
First version of the cap path used a stale `previous` bitmask after `clear_residency()`; fixed by resetting `previous = 0`. First version of `lookup` cloned the contract Arc to satisfy the borrow checker; replaced with `let state = &mut *guard` to get disjoint field borrows through the MutexGuard. A test that reused the local name `cache` for two cache instances shadowed the `cache()` helper (E0618); split into two tests. Initial membership-cap test expectations were wrong because the triggering event is now applied after the clear rather than dropped; retraced and set limit to 3.

## Dead Ends
Considered tying edge eviction to digest removal (drop reverse_edges[X] when digest X leaves) plus a pending-edge backstop; rejected as too coupled for the benefit, since pending edges (GPU-stored, not yet offloaded) still grow to the cap in large fleets. Considered reset-on-full for edges (no LRU, zero extra memory); rejected because under high churn it would wipe hot chains every few seconds. Considered keeping `ambiguous` as a flag inside DigestIdentity with `retain` on clear; the separate set is O(1) to clear and lets ambiguous objects be skipped entirely.

## Hints for Future Agents
- No Rust toolchain or protoc was on the machine; user installed rustup (1.96.1 via rust-toolchain.toml) and protobuf. cargo lives at /opt/homebrew/opt/rustup/bin.
- Use `--no-default-features` for dynamo-llm on macOS per AGENTS.md.
- Three dynamo-llm lib tests fail or flake on this Mac without any changes: entrypoint::input::grpc metrics_bind_failure (always), http::service_v2 test_oversized_body_returns_json_413 (flaky), discovery::model_manager disaggregated_pair_sharing_an_alias (only under parallel load).
- Trade-off accepted: a low64 collision where digest A is fully evicted before B arrives is no longer flagged ambiguous. Consequence is a suboptimal hint only; the worker looks up by its own full digest.
- The docs line "Capacity limits can discard evidence and reduce shared-cache hints" already matched this behavior; the old code was stricter than the docs.

## Codebase Discoveries
`update_contract` is called by MooncakeContractWatch::revalidate on every admitted-membership or runtime-config change; same contract only refreshes allowed_sources. `MutexGuard` field borrows are not disjoint; reborrow as `&mut State` first. `lru::LruCache::put` does not return the LRU-evicted entry (`push` does), hence manual `pop_lru`.

## Open Questions
Whether the reviewer prefers LRU over a simpler reset-on-full; LRU was chosen for continuity of hot chains. Whether MAX_DIGEST_IDENTITIES should be dropped now that digests are bounded by memberships (kept to preserve the measured envelope).
